  <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p class="updated">Last updated: [insert date]</p>

  <p>Quizzar Go is developed by an individual developer ("we", "us"). This policy explains what data we collect, why, and how we protect it.</p>
  <p>For privacy questions or requests, contact: <strong>[insert your privacy email]</strong></p>

  <h2>1. Information We Collect</h2>
  <p><strong>Account information</strong></p>
  <ul>
    <li>Google sign-in: name, email, profile picture from your Google account.</li>
    <li>Email sign-up: your email address and a display name we generate automatically (editable later).</li>
    <li>Guest mode (age 13+): an anonymous account with no personal information attached, used to sync your progress across app sessions.</li>
    <li>Guest mode (under 13): no account is created and no data leaves your device — see Section 6.</li>
  </ul>

  <p><strong>Profile picture</strong></p>
  <p>If you upload a custom profile picture, it's stored in our Supabase file storage. We do not share it with any third party.</p>

  <p><strong>Your content</strong></p>
  <ul>
    <li>Quizzes and generated content you save (your "vault") are stored in our Supabase database, tied to your account.</li>
    <li>Chat messages (AI chat / defend features) are stored locally on your device only — never sent to or stored on our servers.</li>
    <li>Documents or images you upload for quiz generation are sent to our AI provider (Google Gemini) for processing only. We do not store them afterward.</li>
  </ul>

  <p><strong>Usage and account data</strong></p>
  <ul>
    <li>Your generation/token balance and usage history.</li>
    <li>Subscription and purchase status.</li>
    <li>Basic usage data used only for rate limiting and abuse prevention.</li>
  </ul>

  <p><strong>Advertising data</strong> <em>(once ads are live in the app)</em></p>
  <ul>
    <li>Google AdMob may collect device/advertising identifiers, IP address, and app usage to serve ads and verify ad-reward claims. This does not apply to users who indicate they are under 13 — see Section 6.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>2. How We Use Your Information</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To provide core features: quiz generation, saving, and syncing across your devices.</li>
    <li>To manage your account, subscription, and generation balance.</li>
    <li>To prevent abuse (rate limiting, purchase fraud checks).</li>
    <li>To improve the app.</li>
    <li>To serve ads and verify ad-reward claims <em>(once live)</em>.</li>
  </ul>
  <p><strong>We do not sell your personal information.</strong></p>

  <h2>3. Advertising</h2>
  <p>The free version of Quizzar Go may display ads served by Google AdMob, and offers optional rewarded ads in exchange for bonus generations.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Age-based ad treatment:</strong> We use Google's age-treatment signal (TFAT) to tell Google how to treat ad requests for each user. Users who indicate they are under 13 at signup are never shown personalized ads — only non-personalized, contextual ads.</li>
    <li><strong>Consent (EEA/UK/Switzerland and certain US states):</strong> Where required, we present a consent choice through Google's User Messaging Platform (UMP) before showing ads. You can grant, withhold, or change your consent for personalized advertising at any time in Settings &rarr; Privacy Choices.</li>
    <li><strong>Technical ad data:</strong> Google AdMob may collect device identifiers (such as IP address, device model, and OS version) to deliver, report on, and secure ads. Learn more at <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google's Privacy &amp; Terms</a> and <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" target="_blank" rel="noopener">how Google uses information from apps that use our services</a>.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>4. Who We Share Data With</h2>
  <table>
    <tr><th>Service</th><th>What it receives</th><th>Purpose</th></tr>
    <tr><td>Supabase</td><td>Account data, profile picture, vault/generated content, usage data</td><td>Backend hosting, authentication, database, file storage</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Google (Gemini API)</td><td>Quiz-generation prompts, uploaded documents/images (not stored after processing)</td><td>AI-generated content</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Google Play Billing</td><td>Purchase and subscription events</td><td>Payment processing — we never receive your card details</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Google AdMob <em>(once live)</em></td><td>Device/advertising identifiers, app usage</td><td>Ad serving and ad-reward verification</td></tr>
  </table>
  <p>Supabase is our infrastructure provider — data stored there remains ours and is not sold or independently used by Supabase, but we disclose it here for transparency since it is a data processor.</p>

  <h2>5. Payments</h2>
  <p>Subscriptions are purchased and processed entirely through Google Play Billing. We never see or store your payment card details — only a transaction ID and subscription status, used to manage your account entitlement.</p>

  <h2>6. Children's Privacy</h2>
  <p>Quizzar Go is not directed at children under 13. We ask for your age when you create an account or start a guest session.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Account creation</strong> is blocked entirely for anyone who indicates they are under 13.</li>
    <li><strong>Guest mode for under-13 users</strong> does not create any account and does not transmit any data off your device — no analytics, no sync, no ad targeting.</li>
    <li><strong>Advertising</strong> shown to any under-13 user is limited to non-personalized, contextual ads only, signaled via Google's age-treatment system (see Section 3).</li>
    <li>We do not knowingly collect personal information from children under 13. If we learn we've done so in error, we will delete it. Parents who believe their child has provided us data can contact us at [privacy email] to request deletion.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>7. Your Rights</h2>
  <p>Depending on where you live, you may have the right to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Access the personal data we hold about you</li>
    <li>Correct inaccurate data</li>
    <li>Delete your account and associated data</li>
    <li>Export your data</li>
    <li>Object to or restrict certain processing</li>
    <li>(California residents) Know what categories of data we collect, and opt out of any sale — we do not sell data</li>
  </ul>
  <p>You can delete your account directly in the app under <strong>Settings &rarr; Delete Account</strong>, or by contacting us at [privacy email].</p>

  <h2>8. Data Retention</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Account, profile, and vault data is retained only while your account is active.</li>
    <li>Chat history stays on your device only and is never sent to us.</li>
    <li><strong>When you delete your account, we delete your data immediately</strong> — profile, avatar, vault content, and usage data are removed from our live systems as soon as your deletion request is processed. A copy may persist for up to 30 days in encrypted system backups before being fully purged, as part of our standard backup retention cycle.</li>
    <li><strong>Subscription and payment records are the one exception</strong> — we retain a snapshot of your subscription history (including a copy of your email address at the time of deletion) permanently, even after your account is deleted. This is required for accounting, tax, and fraud-prevention purposes, and to resolve payment disputes if they arise. No other personal data is retained after deletion.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>9. International Users</h2>
  <p>We use service providers (Supabase, Google) that may process data outside your country, including in the United States. By using the app, you consent to this transfer.</p>

  <h2>10. Security</h2>
  <p>We use reasonable technical measures (encrypted storage, access controls, row-level database security) to protect your data, but no system is 100% secure.</p>

  <h2>11. Changes to This Policy</h2>
  <p>We'll notify you of material changes via an in-app notice and update the "Last updated" date above.</p>

  <h2>12. Contact</h2>
  <p>[insert privacy email]</p>
